WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:04.182
Eh, you know the DPLL solver coming in the next lesson?

2
00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:06.262
It cannot read arrows one.

3
00:00:06.282 --> 00:00:08.772
Give it if P then Q, it blur.

4
00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:13.068
It only eats ONE shape: an AND of ORs.

5
00:00:13.088 --> 00:00:16.698
That shape is CNF, clause normal form.

6
00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:18.672
So today, 3 things lah.

7
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:20.592
What CNF is exactly.

8
00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:24.592
The 5 steps that turn ANY formula into CNF, always the

9
00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:28.752
same order. And the traps where people lose marks, especially 1

10
00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:30.432
fellow called De Morgan.

11
00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:32.912
In the exam you get a few formulas and a list

12
00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.872
of clauses, and you tick the clauses that are really in

13
00:00:35.892 --> 00:00:39.022
the CNF. So must be fast and steady.

14
00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:44.821
First the words. A LITERAL is a letter or a negated

15
00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:47.261
letter: P, not Q.

16
00:00:47.281 --> 00:00:51.941
A CLAUSE is literals joined by or: P or not Q

17
00:00:51.961 --> 00:00:56.341
or R. And CNF is clauses joined by and.

18
00:00:56.361 --> 00:00:58.621
AND outside, OR inside.

19
00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:01.261
The other way round, or of ands?

20
00:01:01.281 --> 00:01:04.061
That one is DNF, wrong answer hor.

21
00:01:04.081 --> 00:01:06.701
The course says clause normal form.

22
00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:09.291
Conjunctive normal form, same thing lah.

23
00:01:09.325 --> 00:01:12.785
Now the 5 steps, same ORDER every time.

24
00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.505
Step 1: remove the double arrow.

25
00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:19.785
A if and only if B become: if A then B,

26
00:01:19.805 --> 00:01:22.255
and, if B then A.

27
00:01:22.285 --> 00:01:24.535
Step 2: remove the arrow.

28
00:01:24.685 --> 00:01:28.495
If A then B become: not A or B.

29
00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:32.505
Step 3: push the not inward with De Morgan, and cancel

30
00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.495
double not.

31
00:01:33.645 --> 00:01:36.775
Step 4: distribute or over and.

32
00:01:36.845 --> 00:01:41.225
A or, B and C, become: A or B, and, A

33
00:01:41.245 --> 00:01:41.975
or C.

34
00:01:42.285 --> 00:01:44.695
Step 5: read off the clauses.

35
00:01:44.847 --> 00:01:46.187
Why this order ah?

36
00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:48.987
Because a not cannot walk through an arrow.

37
00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:51.257
So the arrows must go FIRST.

38
00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.407
Okay, 1 library rule.

39
00:01:55.427 --> 00:01:57.567
P: you may borrow.

40
00:01:57.587 --> 00:02:00.047
Q: you got unpaid fine.

41
00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.527
R: you got overdue book.

42
00:02:02.547 --> 00:02:07.117
The rule: P if and only if not, Q or R.

43
00:02:07.191 --> 00:02:11.171
Step 1: split the double arrow into 2 arrows, one for

44
00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:15.211
each direction. Step 2: kill both arrows.

45
00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:19.051
Left half: not P, or not, Q or R.

46
00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:22.771
Right half: not not, Q or R, or P.

47
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:25.371
Step 3: push the nots in.

48
00:02:25.391 --> 00:02:29.811
Left half, De Morgan: not, Q or R, become not Q

49
00:02:29.831 --> 00:02:33.731
AND not R. The or flip to and, and BOTH get

50
00:02:33.751 --> 00:02:37.971
a not. Right half, the not not cancel: Q or R

51
00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:41.571
or P. Step 4: distribute the left half.

52
00:02:41.591 --> 00:02:45.811
Not P or not Q, and, not P or not R.

53
00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:47.731
Step 5: read off.

54
00:02:47.751 --> 00:02:50.771
3 clauses. Not P or not Q.

55
00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:52.571
Not P or not R.

56
00:02:52.591 --> 00:02:54.291
P or Q or R.

57
00:02:54.311 --> 00:02:55.641
Done already lah.

58
00:02:55.799 --> 00:02:58.398
The order inside a clause no matter one.

59
00:02:58.418 --> 00:03:00.051
Compare clauses like SETS.

60
00:03:00.071 --> 00:03:03.211
And every step keeps the same truth table, so a table

61
00:03:03.231 --> 00:03:05.041
can always check your answer.

62
00:03:07.191 --> 00:03:10.841
Now the traps. Trap 1, De Morgan.

63
00:03:10.871 --> 00:03:14.771
Not, P or Q, is NOT the clause not P or

64
00:03:14.791 --> 00:03:19.651
not Q. The or must flip: not P AND not Q.

65
00:03:19.671 --> 00:03:21.851
That is 2 unit clauses!

66
00:03:21.871 --> 00:03:25.011
Forget the flip, 1 sign wrong, and the exam got that

67
00:03:25.031 --> 00:03:26.933
wrong clause waiting for you.

68
00:03:26.953 --> 00:03:30.613
Trap 2: not, if P then Q.

69
00:03:30.633 --> 00:03:32.893
Cannot just push the not inside.

70
00:03:32.913 --> 00:03:36.853
Remove the arrow first: not, not P or Q.

71
00:03:36.873 --> 00:03:39.657
Then De Morgan: P and not Q.

72
00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:43.337
Trap 3: a knowledge base with many sentences.

73
00:03:43.357 --> 00:03:47.417
Convert each sentence ALONE, then put all the clauses in 1

74
00:03:47.437 --> 00:03:52.537
set. And for entailment with DPLL, negate the question first, then

75
00:03:52.557 --> 00:03:53.367
convert.

76
00:03:53.814 --> 00:03:58.937
So remember: CNF is AND of ORs, 5 steps, arrows go

77
00:03:58.957 --> 00:04:03.737
first. The practice notebook got 6 exercises: spot what is already

78
00:04:03.757 --> 00:04:07.497
CNF, name the rule, find the wrong step, and a small

79
00:04:07.517 --> 00:04:10.407
checker that compares your clauses with the truth table.

80
00:04:10.557 --> 00:04:13.497
Graded work must be your own hor, the course does not

81
00:04:13.517 --> 00:04:15.687
allow AI there. Jia you!
